codex
The new logical_id migration guard can be bypassed with valid SQLite schema-qualified names for the protected canonical tables, allowing banned migrations to pass the guard. The tests added in the patch do not cover this SQL shape.

Review comment:

- [P2] Handle schema-qualified canonical table names — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s25/src/rust/crates/fathomdb-schema/src/lib.rs:1237-1238
  When a migration schema-qualifies the table (for example `UPDATE main.canonical_nodes SET logical_id = ...` or `INSERT INTO main.canonical_nodes(logical_id) ...`), SQLite targets the same pinned table, but the guard compares the extracted token literally against `CANONICAL_NODES`/`CANONICAL_EDGES`. The token becomes `MAIN.CANONICAL_NODES`, so the new pin silently accepts the exact backfill shape it is meant to reject; normalize or strip an optional schema prefix before this comparison.
